    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "C. PARSONS DEL\nBREADTH OF BEAM\nDIMENSIONe\nSalared according to and of Congress in the year 1854 6y N. Cursis in the Clash Of of the Dished Court of Nam Yond\nCLIPPER SHIP \"NIGHTINGALE\nGetting under weigh off the Battery. New York\nNEW YORK PURLISHED RY N CURRIER 1E MACCATE CODERY\nTONNAGE PER REGISTER\nLITH. BY N. CURRIER",
      "Pan Am.\nSherry\nDubonnet\nCampari\nNoilly Prat\nManhattan\nGin Martini\nVodka Martini\nBloody Mary\nScrewdriver\nWhiskey Sour\nTom Collins\nVodka Collins\nScotch\nBourbon\nCanadian\nGin\nVodka\nRum\nBeer\nWine of Burgundy\nWine of Bordeaux\n-from the wine cellars of our Inter-Continental Hotels\nChampagne\nCointreau\nDrambuie\nBénédictine\nCreme de Menthe\nCognac VSOP\nBénédictine and Brandy\n465 J\n190",
      "HORS D'OEUVRE\nA display of specialties from various countries\nENTREES\nGrilled Lamb Chops\nRoast Striploin of Kobe Beef\n-212-\nSauteed Chicken - Celery and Prawns -Black Bean Sauce\n*0****\nBraised Salmon in Champagne Sauce with Boiled Parslied Potatoes\nButtered Garden Vegetables\nwhit as\nSteamed Japanese Rice\n917\nDauphine Potatoes\nSelection of Cheese\nCherries Jubilee-Vanilla Ice Cream Cookies\nAmerican Coffee\nOrange Pekoe Tea\nJapanese Green Tea\nHA*\n465 JA CC (3291) 5/73\n1997.59.39.04",
      "CLIPPER SHIP \"NIGHTINGALE'\nThe front cover of this menu is a reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives clipper ship print.\nCurrier \u0026 Ives, known as the \"Printmakers of America\", graphically preserved the glorious chpper\nship era in a magnificent series of clipper ship prints. This print, one of a series, 1s being reproduced\nthrough the courtesy of The Mariners Museum, Newport News, Virginia.\nThe clipper ship \"Nightingale\" was named in honor of Jenny Lind, the \"Swedish Nightingale,\"\nwhose golden voice had recently enchanted America. The \"Nightingale\" was considered one of the\nmost beautiful of all the \"American clippers. She was built to be exhibited at the World's faul\nto be held in London, in 1851, as an example of the magnificent skill and craftsmanship of the\n\"Yankee\" shipbuilders. No expense was spared in her design and construction and she proudly\ncarried a life size carving of the \"Swedish Nightingale\" as her ship's figurehead. She started service\ncarrying passengers to and from the World's Fair in London and later was used on the Australiar\nrun where she established such sailing records as going from Melbourne to New York in to days.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers* of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the lanes of com-\nmerce to all the far places of the world... to Japan ... to Australia... and, in the days of the\ngreat gold rush, from America's east coast, around Cape Horn, South America, to California\nOur current equipment... the Clipper fleet of the Twentieth Century... consists of the finest\ncommercial aircraft ever developed-aircraft that have helped us establish an unparalleled record\nfor satety, speed and service.\n•CLIPPER TRADE MARK-REG US PAT OFFICE - COPYRIGHT 1966 PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS INC\nLITHO IN USA-8739-039"
    ],
